+     * never maps anything else this way, and nothing outside PPL writes these
+     * pages, so boot behaves as on hardware; only the (emulation-irrelevant) PPL
+     * write-protection of otherwise-idle pages is relaxed. Kernel text (XN=0)
+     * and EL0 mappings are untouched. This is inert on a non-Apple core because
